al porting."},{"issue_number":7,"action":"comment","comment_body":"Add explicit acceptance criteria:\n1. `__getitem__(i)` returns `(x_context, y_target)` where `x_context.shape == (context_len, n_features)` and `y_target.shape == (pred_len, n_features)`.\n2. When `i < context_len - 1`, the context window is zero-padded at the start (consistent with existing `StockDatasetRNN`).\n3. The class works with `torch.utils.data.DataLoader`.\n4. A factory classmethod `from_array(X, y, context_len, pred_len)` for numpy input.\n\nAlso clarify: is `y_target` the immediate next `pred_len` steps after `x_context`, or is there a stride/hop parameter?"},{"issue_number":8,"action":"comment","comment_body":"Clarify three points:\n1. Should stub classes inherit from `EncoderDecoderForecaster` (issue #6)? If so, this issue is blocked by #6.\n2. Does this issue delete the old `neural_network/` and `probabilistic/` directories, or was that handled in #3 and #4? If not handled yet, add directory deletion here.\n3. This cycle contains no issues for the actual model refactors (LSTM→LSTMForecaster, GRU→GRUForecaster, etc.). Is that intentional? If so, note explicitly that only stubs are in scope for this cycle.\n\nAcceptance criterion: `from stockpy.forecasters import LSTMForecaster` succeeds (stub class)."},{"issue_number":9,"action":"comment","comment_body":"The body is empty. Please specify the transform API design:\n1. sklearn-style (`fit`, `transform`, `inverse_transform`) or plain callables?\n2. numpy arrays or torch tensors?\n3. Integration with `TimeSeriesDataset` — passed as a `transform=` argument or applied before dataset creation?\n\nAcceptance criterion: `Normalizer().fit(X).transform(X)` and `Differencer().transform(X)` produce outputs whose shapes are compatible with `TimeSeriesDataset` from issue #7."},{"issue_number":10,"action":"ok","comment_body":""},{"issue_number":11,"action":"ok","comment_body":""},{"issue_number":12,"action":"ok","comment_body":""}]}
